          "question": "my dads left arm has gone all achy n hes gone grey and sweaty, hes 62, is that somethin to worry about",
          "answer": "**Please call emergency services now (999 in the UK, 911 in the US, or your local number).** Don't wait to see if it passes.\n\nA sore left arm, grey skin and sweating can be signs of a possible heart attack. The chest pain guidance (red-flag-chest-pain) says that discomfort spreading to one or both arms, together with a cold sweat, is treated as a possible heart attack until proven otherwise, and that this needs an emergency call. I can't tell from here what is causing this, and only a clinician can. My automatic check returned a \"routine\" result, but that check only matches a fixed list of patterns and does not clear your dad. Don't rely on it.\n\nWhile you wait for help:\n- Keep him sitting or lying down and calm.\n- Don't let him walk around or drive himself anywhere.\n- Loosen tight clothing.\n- If he has been prescribed heart medicine such as nitroglycerin, follow the instructions he already has. Don't give anything new without advice from the call handler.\n\nIf he becomes unconscious or stops breathing normally, tell the call handler straight away.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
